# Every text file is LF, in the repository and in every checkout.
#
# Windows git defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which checks text out as CRLF.
# Prettier's own default is LF, so a checkout that gets formatted or checked
# with a config that does not say `endOfLine: "auto"` fails on line endings
# alone (QA-054); CI on Linux never saw it. Saying it here takes the decision
# away from each machine's git config.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Detection already treats these as binary; naming them means a font or image
# that happens to look like text is never "normalised" into a broken file.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
